invariant: INV-24
file: x25519.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh x25519_tail
reason: dropping one of mul's two carry passes leaves limb 0 holding the
  top limb's fold, far outside (-2^17, 2^17), the range every x25519
  field-op proof assumes and mul's narrowing to int32 relies on. bin/unit
  fails on it too, once that narrowing truncates; the violation checks
  that the proof sees the bound on its own, at 2^17, where the vectors
  notice a limb only past 2^31
  (https://github.com/c4milo/chapulin/pull/117 measured 4 of
  x25519_tail's 458 properties failing). Each run is a proof of minutes,
  so this belongs to the nightly's full test-invariants, never the fast
  tier.

--- old
    carry(o);
    carry(o);
}
--- new
    carry(o);
}
